Establishment of a dynamic purchasing system (DPS) for the procurement of measuring instruments, measurement tools and associated services 1 - Antenna signal path switches, active monitoring antennas 15 pc(s) of antenna signal path switches controllable via LAN interface 15 pc(s) of broadband switchable active monitoring antennas; 2 - Low-noise compressors 3 pc(s) of low-noise compressors; 3 - Electric generators 3 pc(s) of electric generators; 1 - Field strength measuring probe 1 number of field strength measuring probes as specified in the technical description.; 2 - Real-time spectrum analyser 1 number of real-time spectrum analysers as specified in the technical description.; The network of radiomonitoring measuring stations is to be expanded by the procurement of • 5 number of radiomonitoring and direction-finding stations, • 5 number of SBCs capable of supporting machine learning, and • 5 number of specially designed measurement control computers according to the uploaded technical description.; 1 - Measuring receiver 1 pc(s) of measuring receivers as specified in the technical description.; 2 - Measurement control software and hardware As detailed in the attached technical description: • 1 number of measurement control software for real-time monitoring purposes • 1 number of measurement control tablets • 1 number of measurement control computers.; 3 - Radio frequency measuring heads Procurement of radio frequency measuring heads as specified in the technical description: • 1 number of Radio frequency magnetic measuring heads • 1 number of Low-frequency electric field strength measuring heads • 1 number of Low-frequency magnetic measuring heads; 4 - Calibration kit It is the Tenderer's task to renew and extend the hardware and software supports related to the software and measuring instruments below for an additional duration of 12 months. Handing over to the Contracting Authority of the manufacturer's statement or a statement originating from the manufacturer's representative in Hungary certifying the support belonging to the given device or software licence. Extension of software maintenance for one year for 4 pc(s) of MetroNID GT-G AC type IP network demarcation device with expiry date of 2025.01.22. Extension of software maintenance for one year for 2 pc(s) of MetroNODE LT -SG type IP network demarcation device with expiry date of 2025.01.22.; 5 - Expansion of Spirent test centre measurement capabilities Expansion of Spirent test centre measurement capabilities as specified in the technical description: • 1 number of Spirent C50 Wi-Fi analyser port expansion • Spirent Test Center training.; 6 - Data loggers Data loggers according to the technical description: • 2 number of temperature and humidity data loggers.; 2 pc(s) of NetAlly AirCheck G2 Wifi tester Gold Support software maintenance • 2 pc(s) of NetAlly AirMagnet Wifi Analyzer PRO Gold Support software maintenance • 2 pc(s) of NetAlly AirMagnet Spectrum XT Gold Support software maintenance; • 2 pc(s) of extension of software maintenance of Krypto 500 decoding software • 2 pc(s) of extension of software maintenance of Krypto 1000 decoding software; • 1 pc(s) of extension of software maintenance of IXIA IxChariot; • 1 pc(s) of 12-month warranty extension belonging to DVB-S/S2/S2X/T systems • 1 pc(s) of 12-month software and hardware warranty extension belonging to DVB-C system • 1 pc(s) of software maintenance of alarm and recording management system; • 1 pc(s) of software maintenance of CRFS RFeye Site measurement control software • 1 pc(s) of software maintenance of CRFS TDOA measurements plug-in module (module under RFeye Site) • 2 pc(s) of renewal of CRFS AOA measurements licence • 1 pc(s) of software maintenance of SVALE SpecView signal processing software • 34 pc(s) of software maintenance of CRFS NCP Premium embedded module • 44 pc(s) of software maintenance of SVALE SV-BIM1 extended spectrum image recording processing module • 44 pc(s) of software maintenance of SVALE WebGUI status indicator, rotator control and result display module • 1 pc(s) of software maintenance of SVALE SV-UAP1 measurement control, data processing and display Windows desktop application • 1 pc(s) of software maintenance of measurement environment control module software components of SVALE SV-UAC1; • 4 pc(s) of software maintenance of MetroNID GT-G AC type IP network demarcation device • 2 pc(s) of software maintenance of MetroNODE LT -SG type IP network demarcation device; It is the Tenderer's task to supply 2 pc(s) of measuring receivers for real-time monitoring purposes, as well as to interface the devices to be delivered to 2 pc(s) of servers provided by the Contracting Authority, while implementing continuous 24-hour I/O recording with a sliding window. The software integration of the measuring receivers into the Contracting Authority's existing servers is prescribed in the following manner: • Be capable of real-time reception, FFT processing, display, and forwarding − towards other devices − via Ethernet interface of the VITA-49 format I/Q data stream at the data output of the measuring receiver; • Be capable of continuous recording and storage of the incoming I/Q data stream going back at least 24 hours − alongside maximum IF bandwidth − and enable moving-window buffering of the incoming I/Q data stream with 2 x 100 MHz bandwidth; • Be capable of displaying a resolution bandwidth of at least 100 Hz in the case of a signal with 500 MHz IF bandwidth; • API-based remote control covering full functionality via Ethernet interface must be ensured, for which the Tenderer must enclose a comprehensive documentation package; • Have an independent, OpenGL-based graphical control interface supporting all functionalities of the measuring device (with a spectrum image drawing frequency of at least 60 Hz); • There must be an option for channel power calculation, as well as bandwidth determination based on the ITU-R SM.443 recommendation; • Be capable of simultaneous measurement on at least 6 virtual channels within the real-time bandwidth of the measuring receiver, even while serving multiple users; • There must be an option for demodulation from the incoming VITA-49 format I/Q data stream in the case of at least the following modulations: AM, FM, WFM+RDS, USB, LSB, CW; • Be capable of zero-span operation; • Be capable of real-time frequency excision from the incoming VITA-49 format I/Q data stream and forwarding the bands thus created as a data stream; • GNSS-based route registration measurement capability must be supported alongside the use of an integrated GNSS receiver unit;

• Warranty at least 36 months. A detailed technical description can be found in the procurement documents.; 1. Portable broadband direction-finding system (1 pieces) The tenderer's task is to supply 1 pieces of broadband, calibrated, portable measuring systems with direction-finding capability and real-time mode, ensuring the performance of the contracting authority's interference investigation tasks. Other requirements: • Must be controllable via a LAN interface; • Must have detailed user and programming (SCPI) manuals; • Must have the capability to transmit VITA 49 format I/O and spectrum data as a data stream; • Must have an external 12 V DC vehicle power charging adapter; • Must have at least 4 spare batteries, as well as a battery charger for charging the spare batteries (outside the instrument); • Must have a harness suitable for carrying on the upper body; • The instrument must be waterproof or its case must be rainproof (at least IP 54 protection); • Must have a lockable case or bag for transport and storage purposes, in which hand-held antennas can also be placed in addition to the base instrument; • Must have a lockable case for transport and storage purposes, in which the direction-finding antenna system can be placed; • The direction-finding antenna system must have at least one 5 metre and one 15 metre long control and RF cable; • Must have a manufacturer's calibration certificate; • Warranty at least 24 months. 2. Broadband direction-finding system mountable in a measurement vehicle (2 pieces) The tenderer's task is to supply 2 pieces of broadband, calibrated measuring systems mountable in a rack frame, integrable into a measurement vehicle, with direction-finding capability and real-time mode, ensuring the performance of the contracting authority's interference investigation tasks. Other requirements: • Must be controllable via a LAN interface; • Must have detailed user and programming (SCPI) manuals; • Must have the capability to transmit VITA 49 format I/O and spectrum data as a data stream; • Must have an external 12 V DC vehicle power charging adapter; • For the purpose of fixed installation, the direction-finding antenna system must have a tripod antenna mount, as well as a composite adapter mountable onto the mount, to which the direction-finding antenna system can be securely fastened; • The combined length of the tripod antenna mount and the composite adapter must be at least 2,5 metres high in the open position; • Must have a lockable case for transport and storage purposes, in which the tripod antenna mount can be placed; • The direction-finding antenna system must also have at least one 5 metre and one 15 metre long control and RF cable; • Must have a manufacturer's calibration certificate; • Warranty at least 24 months. 3. Measurement data processors for direction-finding systems (3 pieces) The tenderer's task is to supply 3 pieces of measurement data processors for the direction-finding systems, ensuring the performance of the contracting authority's interference investigation tasks. Other requirements: • Must have a TPM 2.0 module, a watchdog timer, and an external fan cooling accessory; • Must have an external (230V) power supply; • Sample product: OnLogic Karbon 803; • Warranty at least 24 months. A detailed technical description can be found in the procurement documents.; The tenderer's task is to supply 5 pieces of monitoring-purpose measuring stations with direction-finding capability for the contracting authority. The stations must include the following components and antennas (relating to 1 measuring stations): • 1 pcs directional rotatable antennas; • 1 pcs antenna rotators and the associated rotation control module; • 1 pcs high-gain GNSS antennas and the associated feed module; • 1 pcs lower-band monitoring antennas; • 1 pcs upper-band monitoring antennas; • 1 pcs direction-finding antennas with the associated control cable; • 1 pcs 5G capable router with the associated receiving antenna also suitable for receiving 5G and GNSS signals; • 1 pcs measurement control computers; • 1 pcs SBC capable of supporting machine learning; • 2 pcs measuring receivers with an IF bandwidth of at least 40 MHz each, with direction-finding capability for one of the receivers; • 1 pcs GNSS receiving antennas with the associated intelligent feed and signal splitting unit (hereinafter signal splitter); • 3 pcs SPDT type RF signal path switch switchable from 1 to 2. Assembly includes the installation of the main units into the measuring station housing, the establishment of the internal structured IP network, the implementation of the power supply system necessary for the operation of the devices to be built in, and the creation of other control and internal RF signal paths necessary for the operation of the measuring station. Requirements set for the monitoring-purpose measuring station with direction-finding capability to be supplied to the contracting authority: 1. Requirements set for the measuring station: The measuring station must contain 2 pcs independent measuring receivers, of which at least one receiver must have direction-finding capability. 2. Establishing the integrability of the measuring station into the contracting authority's IT system: To be integrated into the contracting authority's IT system, the measuring station must have a 4G LTE and 5G NR capable communication interface. The communication interface must be located within the measuring station housing. The availability of the measuring station must be ensured via an IPsec VPN connection. 3. Establishing the integrability of the measuring station into the contracting authority's measuring system: To be integrated into the contracting authority's measuring system, the measuring station must have a measurement control computer and a single-board computer (SBC) capable of supporting machine learning. The computer and the SBC must be located within the measuring station housing. A detailed technical description can be found in the procurement documents.; The contracting authority performs its spectrum monitoring tasks primarily with the help of its fixed measuring stations and measurement vehicles.

In addition to those listed, it also features a special measurement system (UAV measurement system), which provides the capability to perform radio frequency measurements from the air, thereby making it possible to examine the antenna directional characteristics of radio transmitters and to support radio interference hunting from the air. The "UAV measurement system" is a box/container that can be attached to an unmanned aerial vehicle, housing a radio frequency measuring instrument, an onboard computer, a navigation system, and a battery providing independent power supply. Various measuring antennas can be attached to the measurement system thus formed, with which the listed measurement activities can be carried out in the frequency range of 20–6000 MHz. The aim of the procurement is to modernise the metrology service's current UAV measurement system. Measuring instruments and equipment to be delivered to the Contracting Authority: - The RF measuring unit and the associated measurement control/signal processing unit: 1 pcs of RF measuring units, as well as the associated 1 pcs of measurement control/signal processing units and their accessories; - 2 pcs of U.FL - SMA type patch cables compatible with the antenna connectors of the RF measuring unit; - RF data communication link and stands: 1 pcs of onboard transceiver equipment according to the specification below, as well as the associated 1-1 pcs of ground station transceiver equipment and their accessories; - High-performance 5G capable router: procurement of 2 pcs of 5G capable routers meeting the specification; - Batteries and battery charger: 6 pcs of batteries according to the specification, as well as 1 pcs of battery chargers used for charging them. A detailed technical description can be found in the procurement documentation.; 5 pieces of personal exposimeters; 1 pieces of small broadband electromagnetic field strength meters; 2 pieces of thermal power sensor heads 2 pieces of average power sensor heads; The Tenderer's task is to renew and extend the software and hardware and software supports related to the measuring instruments below for an additional period of 12 months. Handing over to the Contracting Authority a declaration proving the support belonging to the given device, software licence, originating from the manufacturer or the manufacturer's Hungarian representative. Extension of the software support of 4 pcs of MetroNID GT-G AC type IP network demarcation devices with an expiry date of 2025.01.22 by one year. Extension of the software support of 2 pcs of MetroNODE LT -SG type IP network demarcation devices with an expiry date of 2025.01.22 by one year.; 1 pieces of MIMO channel emulator type special RF generators; • 1 pieces of single-channel microwave mixing units • 1 pieces of bandpass filters • 1 pieces of driver amplifiers; • 6 pieces of microwave electric sensor heads • 2 pieces of low-frequency magnetic sensor heads • 1 pieces of combined electric and magnetic sensor heads; • 1 pieces of verification kits for 2.4mm connectors • 1 pieces of verification kits for 2.92mm connectors • 1 pieces of verification kits for 3.5mm connectors • 1 pieces of verification kits for 75 Ohm N connectors; • 1 pairs of circular Helmholtz coils • 1 pieces of circular measuring coils • 1 pieces of Hall sensors • 1 pieces of function generators • 1 pieces of power amplifiers • 1 pieces of compensation networks • 1 pieces of programmable DC power supplies • 1 pieces of six and a half digit multimeters • 1 sets of measuring accessories • 1 measuring software; 1 pcs of short-wave direction-finding devices installable on measuring motor vehicles; Supply of a total of 18 pcs of software component licences capable of decoding the parameters detailed in the Technical Description of 2G, 4G, and 5G mobile networks.; Procurement of a measurement system for solar inverters and their accessory units according to the following, as well as those detailed in the technical description: Bidirectional programmable direct current power supply (2 pcs) Solar panel simulation software (1 pcs) Battery simulation software (1 pcs) Symmetrical direct current impedance stabilisation network (DC-LISN) (1 pcs) Common mode absorbing device (CMAD) (3 pcs) Impedance stabilisation network for RJ45 wire pairs (ISN) (1 pcs) Regenerative AC electronic load and grid simulator for off-grid and on-grid type inverters (1 pcs); Within the framework of the procurement, the following development will be implemented: • 4 pieces of high-precision GNSS receivers with their associated antennas • 1 pieces of transceiver equipment operating in repeater mode with the necessary antennas, hardware and software components.; Direction couplers (DBR technical description category 3 item 11: Other RF passive devices) • 1 pcs of direction couplers covering the lower frequency band • 1 pcs of direction couplers covering the upper frequency band Direction couplers having the following characteristics will be required in the future for the regular calibration of NMHH's own instrument park and for other measurements. Direction coupler covering the lower frequency band: • Operating frequency range: from 0,1MHz to 1000 MHz or a broader range • Power tolerance: at least 200W (CW) • Coupling factor: 40dB with a maximum fluctuation of +/-1dB over the entire operating frequency range • Insertion loss: maximum 0,6dB over the entire operating frequency range • Flatness: maximum +/-0,5dB over the entire operating frequency range • Voltage standing wave ratio (VSWR): maximum 1,30:1 over the entire operating frequency range • Directivity: at least 20dB over the entire operating frequency range • Connector type: N female on all four ports • Operating temperature range: from -55°C to +75°C or a broader range Direction coupler covering the upper frequency band: • Operating frequency range: from 1GHz to 18GHz or a broader range • Power tolerance: at least 50W (CW) • Coupling factor: 10dB with a maximum fluctuation of +/-1dB over the entire operating frequency range • Insertion loss: maximum 0,5dB in the range from 1GHz to 6GHz; maximum 0,6dB in the range from 6GHz to 18GHz • Frequency sensitivity: maximum +/-0,7dB in the range from 1GHz to 6GHz; maximum +/-1,0dB in the range from 6GHz to 18GHz • Voltage standing wave ratio (VSWR): maximum 1,35:1 in the range from 1GHz to 6GHz;

at most 1,50:1 in the range from 6 GHz to 18 GHz • Directivity: at least 16 dB in the range from 1 GHz to 6 GHz; at least 12 dB in the range from 6 GHz to 18 GHz • Connector type: SMA female on output; SMA female on input • Operating temperature range: from -40 °C to +85 °C or a broader range *: broader range: here it means that it is acceptable if the lower frequency is lower than 0,1 MHz and/or the upper frequency is higher than 1000 MHz. It is of no significance by how much the offered device's parameter deviates from the prescribed range. Detailed requirements in the procurement documents. During the operation of the DBR, pursuant to Section 107. (2) of the Public Procurement Act, the Contracting Authority shall make the exact technical content and contractual terms concerning the specific procurements to be implemented within the system available to the economic operators participating in the DBR simultaneously with the dispatch of this invitation to tender.; Optical splitter (2 pieces) The measuring instruments ensure measurement accuracy with the help of the NMHH satellite 10 MHz frequency reference. Expansion of this distribution network is necessary in the new metrology building, which must serve multiple endpoints with a reference frequency. This procurement relates to two such devices. Due to the diversity of endpoints, the device must potentially possess both coaxial and optical inputs or outputs. The devices shall be capable of handling a 10 MHz reference frequency with potentially both coaxial and optical connections. Appropriately, taking into account potential future developments, the outputs shall be of a modular design. A rack-mountable design is also a necessary condition. Set technical requirements Inputs: at least 1 pieces of coaxial, with BNC female connector Outputs: at least 18 pieces of optical, modularly interchangeable, with ST connector for 62,5/125 um or 50/125 um multimode cable Maximum optical path length: at least 2 kilometres Design: rack-mountable, half-rack* width (300 x 241,5 x 44,45 mm) Supply voltage: mains 230 V AC *: The standard rack size (300 x 483 x 44,45 mm) is defined based on this. The half-rack size: 300 x 241,5 x 44,45 mm. During the operation of the DBR, pursuant to Section 107. (2) of the Public Procurement Act, the Contracting Authority shall make the exact technical content and contractual terms concerning the specific procurements to be implemented within the system available to the economic operators participating in the DBR simultaneously with the dispatch of this invitation to tender.; Broadband Direction-Finding Antenna (1 pieces) To perform the interference investigation tasks of the Contracting Authority, a modern broadband direction-finding antenna that can also be installed on a measurement vehicle and is compatible with the existing digital direction-finding system (Rohde & Schwarz DDF260) is required with the following characteristics and parameters: Direction-finding frequency range of the antenna: At least: 20 MHz – 7 GHz Polarisation: At least vertical and horizontal Direction-finding accuracy: At most 1.5° RMS Direction-finding sensitivity independently of polarisation: in the range of 50 MHz – 4 GHz at most 10 μV/m in the range of 4 GHz – 7 GHz at most 40 μV/m Standing wave ratio: At most 2.0 Permissible wind speed: At least 150 km/h Other requirements: • Cooperate with the currently used Rohde & Schwarz DDF260 digital direction-finding instrument. • Have a monitoring receiver output in the range of 20 MHz – 7 GHz. • Have a built-in compass and GNSS receiver. • Have lightning protection. • Have an adapter with which its installation on a vehicle can be resolved. • Warranty of at least 36 months due to heavy-duty use.; - Assembly and installation of quasi-fixed/mobile radiomonitoring and direction-finding system: • Development of measuring system in a new vehicle • Reassembly of existing measuring system into a new measurement vehicle • Expansion, modification, dismantling of existing measuring system - Assembly and installation of fixedly installed radiomonitoring and direction-finding stations: • Installation of measuring station o to a new location, o relocation to a new location, o installation at a temporary location, o expansion with new measurement capabilities, o dismantling, decommissioning. - Assembly, installation, expansion, transformation of laboratory measuring stations: • Relocation of existing laboratory measuring system from the current laboratory to the new building. • Development and installation of new laboratory measuring systems in the new building. • Performance of cabling tasks associated with the measuring stations (e.g. connection of power supply, IT and radio frequency signal paths), with the procurement/manufacture of new cables if necessary. • On-site commissioning and functional testing of the measuring system following installation. • Preparation of installation documentation. The documentation must include the description of the measuring station, structural layout, list of measuring instruments and measurement tools, control and data transmission connectivity. • Expansion and transformation of measuring systems in order to implement new measurement capabilities. Installation of measuring tool(s) belonging to the new measurement function. The detailed requirements and expectations pertaining to the necessary equipment relocation, assembly and installation tasks shall also be detailed by the Client to the Contractor in an individual order. • The cost of overhead materials arising during the assembly and installation of the measuring system/measuring station/measuring stations shall be borne by the Contractor. • The removal and disposal, or where necessary destruction, of dismantled and unused cables in accordance with relevant statutory provisions shall be the task of the Contractor. The assembly and installation tasks affect 71 pcs of measuring stations and 21 pcs of measurement vehicles.; 