Full name of the procedure: "Delivery of equipment and teaching aids intended for the implementation of practical classes for the needs of vocational workshops in post-primary schools and the Centre for Vocational Training in Siedlces under the project entitled "Development of modern infrastructure in the field of vocational education in Siedlces", co-financed from the European Regional Development Fund under the European Funds for Mazovia Programme 2021–2027, Priority V „European funds for a higher quality of life in Mazovia”, Measure 5.3 „Infrastructure in vocational education”– part IV: The subject of the contract in this procedure is the delivery of equipment and teaching aids intended for the implementation of practical classes for the needs of vocational workshops in Complex of Post-Primary Schools No. 5 in Siedlces The subject of the contract has been divided into eleven parts: part 1 Modern building technologies workshop part 2 Architectural design workshop part 3 Hair design workshop part 4 Bricklaying and plastering works workshop part 5 Image styling workshop part 6 Dry construction workshop part 7 Hairdressing workshop part 8 Photographic studio part 9 IT part 10 IT - clothing design and production workshop part 11 Software The Contracting Authority allows the submission of partial tenders. The Contractor may submit one tender for any number of parts of the contract. The Contracting Authority does not set a maximum number of parts for which Contractors may submit a tender, or a maximum number of parts for which the contract may be awarded to the same Contractor. The Contractor is obliged to submit a tender covering all items in a given part. A detailed description of the part has been indicated in Appendix No. 1A – Assortment and price form and appendix No. 5 to the ToR – Description of the subject of the contract. The equipment must be delivered to the place of project implementation, i.e., to the Complex of Post-Primary Schools No. 5 in Siedlces named 