sig_c8dffda0a0d0f6fa4ab2.description:
As part of extended funding by the Federal Ministry for Research, Technology and Space (BMFTR), the SoilRob project from the programme area 2 of the Leibniz Centre for Agricultural Landscape Research (ZALF) in Müncheberg is planning to expand existing test equipment and procure new ones. The SoilRob project is working on an integrated understanding of the effects of autonomous small and lightweight agricultural machinery on soils in diversified cropping systems compared to conventional large-scale agricultural machinery. For this purpose, approx. 30 different soil parameters are being investigated for their significance for soil health. In order to further expand existing tests and enable new tests, new test equipment is required. Lot LOT-0001: 1 device Autonomous agricultural robot for mechanical and chemical weed control. - Autonomous agricultural robot for mechanical and chemical weed control with spot-spraying facility, incl. solar modules, for single-grain and cluster sowing as well as RTK-supported weed regulation both in and between the rows. - Energy & drive: Autonomous operation via solar energy (specifically: 4 high-performance solar modules with a total of at least 1,6 kWp). - Core functionality: Fully automatic field robot for at least six-row single-grain and cluster sowing as well as RTK-supported weed regulation both in and between the rows (row spacing is at least 45 cm). - Seeding technology specification: Suitability for seeds up to a maximum of 10 mm in size (incl. seed discs for beet); modified seeding unit with enlarged at least 14 mm seed valve, enlarged chamber and integrated hole punch or similar to prevent seeds from jamming. - Factory-fitted at least 6-row spot sprayer or equivalent - Navigation & precision: High-precision control via RTK-GPS using a base station that transmits the correction signal via the internet - or equivalent - IT & connectivity: Multi-SIM cards for unlimited data volume in all networks; control via app with specific functions for the status of the robot, such as battery status as well as route planning and prediction - Logistics & support: Transport via three-point linkage for field transport - Maintenance package: Spare parts package: Contains matching seed discs, hoeing blades, hoeing wires, seed valves, motors and weights. Further technical data: - Track width: depending on configuration - Working width: depending on configuration - 2x LITHIUM-ION battery 24V, 120Ah, CB, LFP, 120A or equivalent - incl. 1 set of seed discs for beet - Weights for the frame (e.g. 4x 17,5 kg or comparable) - Weights for trailer (e.g. 6 kg per row or comparable) - Weights for the seed pressing roller (e.g. 2 kg per row or comparable) Planning basis: FarmDroid FD20 Design as described or technically equivalent Lot LOT-0002: 1 device Repair and maintenance facility for core sampling technology. The metal drilling and milling machine, with the help of its extensive additional equipment, is a very versatile tool for the maintenance, repair and manufacture of sampling and measuring equipment of all kinds. An example is the repair of core sampling and drilling equipment: in daily operations, impact heads, threads and core sampling tubes are regularly damaged, the repair of which is only possible with carbide-tipped cutters. The technical capability of milling allows, for example, the production of specific adapters (not offered on the market) in order to combine existing drilling or sampling technology with new equipment. This results in significant financial savings and a minimization of time delays in the execution of project tasks. Furthermore, measuring and sampling technology can be adapted directly to specific scientific questions in the current project, e.g. the sampling of extreme soil locations and the production of specific measuring apparatuses (penetrometer cones; housings/installation frames for measuring instruments, soil probes, rhizotrons, etc.). Technical requirements: - Drilling capacity in steel: min. 30 mm - Thread cutting up to M 16 - Spindle head swivel range up to 90° - Spindle taper ISO 40 - Concentricity accuracy less than or equal to 0.015 mm - Quill stroke min. 100 mm - Table size min. 950 x 200 mm - T-slot size min. 14 mm - Table swivelling +/- 45° - Travel x min. 500 mm, y min 160 mm, z min. 300 mm - 3-axis digital readout or equivalent - Automatic milling feed in x and y axes - Machine light - Coolant system - Motor power output min. 1.4 kW Tool equipment: - 1 piece machine vice with min. 150 mm jaw width, turntable and 360° display - 1 piece end mill set (min. 3 to 20 mm) - 1 piece HSS roughing end mill (min. 6 to 25 mm) - 1 piece T-slot cutter set (min. 2 to 10 mm) - 1 piece face and boring head set min. 50 mm MK 2 - 1 piece cutter collet chuck set min. 3 to 25 mm ISO 40 - 1 piece twist drill set HSS with Morse taper min. 14 - 23 mm - 1 piece clamping tool assortment min. 14 mm, M 12 - 1 piece dividing head (indexing device), swivelling up to min. 90°, spindle bore min. 20 mm, direct division 24 (15°), transmission 40:1 or comparable, centre point - 1 canister coolant concentrate 5 Planning basis: Core sounding set 0419SC Design as described or technically equivalent Lot LOT-0003: 1 device Autonomous multi-carrier platform for agricultural technology. Autonomous, highly modular carrier platform with hybrid drive; designed for the integration of a wide range of implements and sensor technology for the automated execution of complex field work under an agri-PV system - Primary energy supply: Diesel engine (approx. 40-45 kW);

an electric motor and batteries for direct energy use from the ZALF agri-PV system are preferred - Drive system including an electric braking system - Active, self-levelling hydraulic chassis - independent 4-wheel steering for maximum manoeuvrability or equivalent - stepless speed of min. 0,5 to 6 km/h - ground clearance of approx. 1,5 m (+/- 0,1 m) for operations in tall crops - unladen weight max. 2.500 kg with a payload of min. 1.500 kg (max. total weight 4.000 kg) - width max. 3 m - height max. 2,4 m - length variable between 4,0 and 5,0 m (depending on the selected main frame length) - Equipped with a hydraulic three-point linkage and additional flange points on the main frame or equivalent - Three-point lifting capacity up to 1.500 kg or more - High-precision positioning using dual RTK-GNSS receiver or similar with heading data and integrated IMU for tilt monitoring - Safety & IT: Long-range safety sensor (min. 5 m) - mechanical safety switching contact strips - min. 2 - 4 x emergency stop button - Geofence monitoring; internet connection via 4G/5G (optional satellite) or equivalent - Operation & software: Wireless remote control for manual operation - graphical web interface via touch display or remote - online portal for machine management incl. mission planning. - Interfaces for Ethernet and CAN for device communication Planning basis: Tipard 2530 from digital workbench Design as described or technically equivalent Lot LOT-0004: 2 devices Attachments for autonomous multi-carrier platform. Consisting of: 1x double-knife mower - Designation: Double-knife mower for use on an autonomous, modular carrier platform under agri-photovoltaic systems - Function and field of application: Attachment for the gentle mowing of lucerne stands as well as other forage and legume stands in agricultural test facilities preferably under agri-PV systems - The mower is particularly suitable for trial plots where uniform cutting performance and low impact on the crop stand are required. - Design: Double-knife mower with counter-reciprocating cutter bars and shearing cutting principle - Working width: Approx. 3,0 m (permissible range 2,8-3,2 m). - Drive: Mechanical, hydraulic or electric drive, suitable for integration into the existing supply and interface systems of the carrier platform. - Cutting height: Adjustable; working range at least 4 to 12 cm. - Requirements for work quality: The mower must guarantee a clean, shearing cut with low plant crushing and minimal leaf losses - Mowing must enable a uniform stubble height over the entire working width - The device must be suitable for repeated cuts in lucerne stands with growth heights of at least 20 to 80 cm. - Operating speed: Suitable for working speeds of 0,5 to 6 km/h. - Weight: Dead weight preferably between 150 and 600 kg. - Special requirements for agri-PV: The overall height and geometry of the device must not restrict passage under agri-PV systems with a clear height of approx. 2 m - Lateral overhangs and protruding components must be designed in such a way that low-collision operation in systems with support posts and module rows is possible. - Safety: All moving components must be equipped with functional protective devices. The device must be suitable for remote-controlled or autonomous operation on an unmanned carrier platform. - Condition: Used device or new device in technically faultless, immediately operational condition. Cutter segments, fingers, bearing points and drive components must not exhibit any damage or impermissible signs of wear that impair functionality. 1x spring-tine cultivator - Designation: Spring-tine cultivator for use on an autonomous, modular carrier platform under agri-photovoltaic systems - Function and field of application: Light to medium-heavy soil cultivation implement for shallow to medium-deep soil cultivation, mechanical weed control, incorporation of crop residues and for seedbed preparation in agricultural test facilities and under agri-PV systems. - Design: Attachment with rigid or foldable frame, suitable for mounting on a hydraulic three-point linkage category I or II or via a technically equivalent interface. - Working width: Approx. 3,0 m (permissible range 2,8-3,2 m). - Tools: At least two rows of bars with spring tines made of spring steel; tines with replaceable shares or duckfoot shares. - Working depth: Continuously adjustable or adjustable in several locking steps - Working range at least 3 to 15 cm. - Requirements for work quality: Uniform cultivation of the entire working width at a working depth of up to 15 cm - The cultivation must enable largely complete cutting of emerged weeds as well as uniform loosening of the topsoil. - Traction requirements: The device must be suitable for use on a carrier platform with a travel speed of min. 0,5 to 6 km/h and a payload of up to 1.500 kg. - Weight: Dead weight preferably between 250 and 800 kg. - Soil adaptation: The design must ensure good contour adaptation under changing soil conditions - The tine suspension must be able to drive over stones and obstacles without damage. - Special requirements for agri-PV: The maximum device height including all components must not impair passage under a clear height of 2m - The device must not have any upwardly projecting components that could lead to collisions with PV modules or substructures.

- Condition: Used device or new device in a technically sound, immediately operational condition - Wearing parts must not exhibit any damage that impairs functionality. Required settings (working depth, cutting height, transport position) must be reproducible and preferably able to be made without tools or with low conversion effort. Execution as described or technically equivalent Lot LOT-0005: 1 Device Four-legged walking robot as a multi-sensor platform. Four-legged walking robot (quadruped) as a mobile platform for autonomous field phenotyping and soil diagnostics; designed for use in open fields and specialised sensor technology applications - Function & Type: Four-legged walking robot (quadruped). Special requirements for sensor integration and research use: The platform must be designed as an open research and development platform and enable the integration, synchronisation and operation of freely developed sensor and data processing applications. The development, calibration and evaluation of specific sensor applications are carried out on a project basis by the client (in-house development within the scope of SoilRob) and are not part of the manufacturer's service. - dust and waterproof - Measurement capabilities: Serves as a base carrier for a multi-sensor system (MSP) - Possibility for integration of LiDAR, camera, thermal and hyperspectral raw data without manufacturer-specific restrictions, capacity of min. 3 processing units with high-computing dock - Size & weight: max 50kg; max 65 cm wide; min. 70 cm high - Energy supply: Operation via a dedicated battery system; set including charger and min. 2 batteries - Operation & IT: Control via remote controller or autonomously via the Robot Operating System (ROS) for the integration of own software modules; support for the integration of LiDAR, camera and GPS data, supports wireless vector positioning; support for georeferenced raw data acquisition (GNSS/IMU) without proprietary processing obligation. - Special characteristics: high customisability through ROS interfaces; open interface architecture such as API, RS485, CAN, Gigabit Ethernet, USB 3.0 Type-C for various sensor setups; - Availability of an intensive support package (2 days training) for on-site commissioning and sensor integration. Planning basis: Quadruped A2 Pro Execution as described or technically equivalent Lot LOT-0006: 1 Device Autonomous agricultural robot for mechanical weed control plus a suitable modem. 1x Modem for already existing Naio Oz - specific retrofit modem kit for the Naio Oz as a remote control replacement to enable complete app-based machine control - Connectivity & Cloud: 4G internet connectivity including access to a secured cloud platform for automatic backup of field maps and system data - Software infrastructure: Including an annual service package for software updates and technical cloud support 1x Autonomous agricultural robot for mechanical weed control Compact, fully electric field robot for mechanical weed control and support with tractive work - Function & type: designed as an autonomous platform for use in specialty crops and research areas (min. 0.5ha/day) - Requires hoeing & harrowing technology for removing weeds in and between the rows for maize, soybeans and other grain legumes - System must be able to remove weeds in the row and between the rows at 75 cm row spacing without damaging the crop (regardless of design (driving between the rows or crop-spanning)) - Navigation & precision: Navigation using a high-precision GNSS RTK receiver or equivalent receiver (system including batteries and charger for the receiver unit) - Control & app connectivity: Control by default via a smartphone or separate remote control - System fully operable via app (e.g., via a specific retrofit modem kit as a remote control replacement or via already integrated internet connectivity) - Connectivity & cloud: min. 4G internet connectivity including access to a secured cloud platform for automatic backup of field maps and system data - Software infrastructure: Including an annual service package for software updates and technical cloud support. - Development & integration: Includes specific R&D services for technical crop-specific adaptation and integration of the modem kit into the existing hardware architecture Optional: - Single-plant treatment: Camera-based AI recognition of crop and weed at the single-plant level; selective mechanical removal in the row - Retrainable AI: Recognition model must be retrainable with small amounts of images for site-specific weeds and crops - Open architecture: Open, documented interfaces (APIs), open-source base components, ROS2 compatibility as well as export of raw data (images, trajectories, mission data) for scientific evaluation - Fleet capability: Central software platform for managing multiple robots and areas incl. mission planning and automatic data backup. - Manufacturer proximity: Crop-specific adaptations and R&D services by the manufacturer itself, with direct access to the development team Planning basis: Naio OZ Execution as described or technically equivalent

