The construction project comprises the general conversion and extension of the central emergency department of SRH Central Hospital Suhl into an integrated emergency centre. The aim of the measure is to adapt and modernise the existing emergency care to meet current functional, medical and operational requirements. To this end, existing building structures will be converted, partially demolished and supplemented by new building areas. In addition, adjustments will be made to the technical infrastructure and the required outdoor facilities. The implementation of the measure will take place while the clinic remains operational and requires close coordination of the construction processes to maintain medical care. Clearing and preparation of the construction site including demolition of paved areas and other exterior components, dismantling of existing roofing, clearing of vegetation and trees, and removal and disposal of topsoil. │approx. 1.800 m2 paved areas and parking deck surfacings, of which approx. 1.270 m2 road concrete slabs and 520 m2 asphalt areas │approx. 150 m2 roofing │approx. 150 m2 grid covers and fall protection systems │approx. 400 m2 clearing and topsoil areas; Extensive partial demolition of the existing structures to prepare for the conversion and new build of the central emergency department. This includes in particular the demolition of the ambulance bay, the existing reinforced concrete ceiling above E01, of facades, walls, doors, windows and floor structures as well as the creation of new openings in the existing building. │1 ambulance bay including adjacent components as total demolition │approx. 1.700 m2 existing ceiling above E01 including floor and roof structures │extensive dismantling of reinforced concrete, masonry and dry construction walls │dismantling of existing facades, windows, exterior doors, gates and interior doors │numerous wall and ceiling breakthroughs for the reorganization of the building; Construction of the new two-storey structure on levels E01 and E02 as a reinforced concrete skeleton structure integrating the remaining existing components. The services include earthworks and foundation work, underfillings, foundations, reinforced concrete walls, columns, beams, ceilings and stairs as well as supplementary masonry and steel construction work. │approx. 250 m3 earthworks │approx. 95 m3 lean concrete underfilling │approx. 530 m2 reinforced concrete exterior walls │approx. 1.700 m2 reinforced concrete ceilings and roof slabs │additionally approx. 60 m strip foundations, pad foundations, columns, beams and masonry walls; Supply and installation of glazed facade structures, ribbon windows and exterior doors including mullion-transom facades, opening vents, sun protection and anti-glare systems as well as associated connection work. │approx. 140 m2 main mullion-transom facade │further mullion-transom and ribbon window constructions │aluminium windows with fixed glazing and opening vents │glazed exterior doors and entrance areas │sun protection, anti-glare and window sill constructions; Construction of the closed, thermally insulated facade areas of the new build and the existing areas to be energetically upgraded, including substructure, facade cladding, insulation and connections to windows, doors and parapets. │facade work within a total exterior wall area of approx. 1.440 m2 │thermal insulation and ventilated substructure │plastered Aquapanel facade areas │connection work to existing building, windows, doors and parapets; Construction of floor structures in the new build and in the existing areas to be converted, including floating and bonded screeds, dry screed, leveling fills, damp-proofing, ramps, dirt-trapping zones and asphalt surfacing in the ambulance bay. │approx. 2.900 m2 screed and floor leveling areas │approx. 1.200 m2 damp-proofing on existing ceilings │dry screed and bonded fills up to approx. 20 cm │approx. 500 m2 asphalt surfacing including substructure in the ambulance bay; Construction of non-load-bearing interior walls, facing shells, installation and shaft walls as well as suspended ceilings. Standard, damp-room, acoustic, fire and radiation protection constructions as well as modular, metal and plasterboard ceilings are included. │approx. 3.300 m2 dry construction walls plus installation, shaft and facing shells │approx. 3.000 m2 suspended plasterboard, modular and metal ceilings; Construction of insulated and waterproofed flat roofs of the new build as well as adaptation and renovation of existing roof areas. Roof waterproofing, sloping insulation, vapour barriers, green roofing, parapets, maintenance walkways, roof domes as well as roof and emergency drainage are included. │total approx. 3.000 m2 roof area │predominantly intensively greened main roof with approx. 37 cm vegetation buildup │roof waterproofing of the ambulance bay and existing roof areas │roof domes, maintenance walkways, gravel edge strips as well as roof and emergency drainage; Supply and installation of exterior and interior doors and gates including fire, smoke, acoustic and radiation protection doors, automatic door systems, sliding doors and roller shutters. │extensive interior door systems for approx. 5.650 m2 gross floor area │fire and smoke protection doors │radiation protection doors for X-ray and CT areas │automatic sliding and revolving door systems │roller and sectional doors for access and functional areas; Manufacture and installation of metalwork and locksmith constructions including railings, handrails, fall protection systems, roof access ladders, privacy screen elements and edge protection. │approx. 250 m stair and fall protection systems │roof access including ladder construction │privacy screen elements at the ambulance bay │approx. 250 m edge protection constructions in heavily used interior areas; Installation of resilient floor coverings in functional, examination, treatment, office, technical and traffic areas including subfloor preparation, dissipative execution, coved skirting boards and connections to the existing building. │approx. 2.500 m2 resilient and predominantly dissipative floor coverings │PVC or rubber coverings in functional and technical areas;

Production of cast stone coverings in stairwells, entrance and waiting areas including stair treads, landings, floor slabs and skirting boards. ─approx. 40 cast stone stair treads ─approx. 40 m2 stair landings ─approx. 190 m2 cast stone coverings in entrance, waiting area and stairwells; production of wall and floor tiles in sanitary, changing and ancillary rooms including substrate preparation, waterproofing and connection work. ─approx. 900 m2 wall tiles ─approx. 200 m2 floor tiles ─bonded waterproofing in wet and sanitary areas; production of wall and ceiling plasters on masonry and concrete surfaces including gypsum and lime-cement plaster, full-surface filling and supplementary internal insulation. ─approx. 2.500 m2 wall and ceiling plaster ─full-surface Q3 finishes ─partial internal insulation with mineral wool; coating of wall and ceiling surfaces in new construction and conversion areas including substrate preparation, coats on plaster, concrete and dry construction surfaces as well as coatings in technical areas. ─approx. 9.600 m2 wall surface coating ─of which approx. 8.000 m2 with non-woven wallpaper ─approx. 1.000 m2 ceiling surfaces ─approx. 800 m2 floor coating; preparatory coating work and coating work brought forward due to the construction schedule on components that are later not accessible or only accessible to a limited extent, in particular above suspended ceilings and behind technical installations. ─650 m2 ceiling coating ─120 m2 floor coatings; production and assembly of fixed interior fittings including wall and edge protection, WC and shower partition walls, lockers, tea kitchens, nursing and monitoring bases as well as other built-in furniture. ─approx. 1.600 m2 wall protection made of hard polyester ─7 WC and shower partition wall systems ─approx. 65 changing lockers ─3 tea kitchens ─2 nursing, control centre and monitoring bases; production of the information, orientation and signage system including markings required by building authorities, door signs, wayfinding and facade lettering. ─approx. 160 door and room markings ─1 facade lettering; supply and installation of the mechanical locking system including profile, double, half, blank and special cylinders as well as adaptation to the clinic's locking concept. ─mechanical lock cylinders for exterior and interior doors ─approx. 100 double and half cylinders ─blank cylinders for non-lockable doors; overarching site installation and site logistics for carrying out the measure during ongoing hospital operations including site security, traffic management, protective measures and jointly used facilities. ─site installation for a building complex with approx. 5.650 m2 gross floor area ─site sign ─approx. 200 m2 construction fence; production, provision and dismantling of the facade, room and stair scaffolding required for facade, roof and interior work. ─approx. 2.100 m2 facade scaffolding from the basement to above the attic ─provision of the facade scaffolding for up to 12 months ─interior scaffolding; construction-accompanying cleaning and protective measures during construction execution as well as final detailed cleaning before commissioning the Central Accident and Emergency Department. ─coarse cleaning for approx. 5.650 m2 gross floor area during the construction period ─protection of already installed floor coverings ─detailed cleaning of approx. 5.650 m2 gross floor area before commissioning; production and restoration of outdoor facilities including earthworks and substructure work, paved traffic, path and recreational areas, barrier-free ramps and stairs, access roads, technical installations, fixtures as well as vegetation and planting areas. ─in total approx. 2.150 m2 outdoor facility area ─paved paths, forecourt and traffic areas ─access roads to the garage hall and service yard ─barrier-free ramps and stair systems ─green and planting areas including trees and shrubs; production of sanitary, heating and refrigeration piping including wastewater and drinking water systems, sanitary fixtures, heat distribution networks, heating surfaces, refrigeration piping as well as fire extinguishing systems. The services also include dismantling, connections to existing networks, insulation, fire protection, fittings, tests and commissioning. ─approx. 800 m wastewater, rainwater, condensate and base lines as well as 2 lifting systems ─approx. 1.650 m drinking water pipes including fittings, insulation and hygiene equipment ─approx. 2.700 m heating pipes as well as heating surfaces and integration into the existing system ─approx. 900 m refrigeration piping including insulation and fittings ─approx. 120 m dry fire extinguishing pipe with 6 extraction points as well as approx. 20 portable fire extinguishers; production of the ventilation and air conditioning systems for the general, medical and infectiological areas of the central accident and emergency department as well as for the statutory health insurance physician and storage area. Included are air conditioning units, fans, duct and pipe networks, air outlets, dampers, volume flow controllers, silencers, insulation, fire protection measures as well as adaptations and dismantling in the existing stock. ─4 ventilation and air conditioning systems with air capacities of approx. 2.100 to 6.750 m3/h ─approx. 500 m circular pipework as well as extensive rectangular air duct and shaped piece surfaces ─approx. 250 air outlets, in particular swirl diffusers, disc valves, grilles and slot outlets ─approx. 85 fire dampers as well as around 200 volume flow controllers and restrictors ─approx. 1.900 m2 heat, condensation and sheet metal jacket insulation including smoke extraction and fire protection cladding; production and integration of building services refrigeration systems including dry coolers, refrigeration distributors, pumps, heat exchangers, circulating air cooling units, hydraulic integration into the existing refrigeration network as well as the associated control, safety and secondary components. ─1 table dry cooler ─1 refrigeration distributors and 1 heat exchangers ─approx. 12 pumps ─5 circulating air cooling units ─approx. 400 m refrigeration pipes including around 200 m refrigeration insulation, fittings and fastenings;

Production of the complete high-voltage power supply for the new emergency department, including safety and battery-backed power supply, main and sub-distribution boards, cable trays and wiring networks, electrical installation, lighting, emergency lighting, room control panels, and connections for technical and medical systems. ─2 main building distribution boards for general and safety power, plus approx. 30 sub- and area distribution boards ─approx. 65.000 m of high-voltage, control and installation cables ─approx. 1.500 switches, sockets and other electrical fittings ─approx. 800 general, safety and emergency exit luminaires; production of the external and internal lightning protection and earthing system, including air-termination systems on roof surfaces, down-conductors, foundation and ring earth electrodes, fixed earthing terminals, connections for metallic components, as well as surge protection and equipotential bonding measures. ─approx. 1.200 m of air-termination conductors on roof surfaces ─approx. 1.100 m of lightning down-conductors including HVI cables ─approx. 700 m of foundation and ring earth electrodes ─approx. 500 earthing and connection components, clamps and connectors ─connections for roof superstructures, metal structures, lifts and stair installations; production and expansion of communication, data and security systems, including telecommunications, DECT, nurse call, clock and sound reinforcement systems, fire alarm systems, site radio, video surveillance, electronic locking and access control systems, passive transmission networks, and active network technology. ─nurse call system with approx. 44 room terminals, around 300 call and reset buttons, and 108 room signal lights ─fire alarm system with 1 fire alarm control panel, approx. 260 automatic detectors, 20 manual call points and 120 brigade route cards ─approx. 480 data outlets, around 950 data connections or patch cables and associated copper and fibre-optic cabling ─50 DECT base stations, 40 WLAN access points and active network components ─electronic locking and access control system with approx. 40 digital locking cylinders, 160 transponders and 4 IP cameras; supply and installation of a bed lift including lift system, cabin and door technology, stainless steel access portals, control system, shaft smoke extraction, fire-incident control, commissioning and documentation. ─1 bed lift system, load capacity approx. 2.500 kg ─cabin dimensions approx. 1,80 × 2,50 m ─2 stainless steel access portals ─1 shaft smoke extraction system including fire-incident control; supply of medical gases and supply and installation of permanently installed medical supply units. This includes pipe networks for oxygen, medical compressed air and vacuum, shut-off, control and alarm devices, extraction points, and wall supply units with electrical and lighting equipment. ─medical gas supply for oxygen, compressed air and vacuum ─approx. 2.000 m of copper pipework DN 6 to DN 40 ─approx. 130 m of pipe dismantling ─extraction points in examination, treatment, resuscitation and procedure rooms ─9 wall supply units for single beds ─2 single-bed luminaires and connections to existing supply networks; production of building and plant automation for the control, regulation, monitoring and visualisation of technical systems. Services include automation stations, room controllers, field devices, switch cabinets, management and operating devices, data point programming, cabling, integration into the higher-level building management system, and commissioning. ─7 automation stations and 7 automation switch cabinets ─approx. 85 room controllers ─approx. 1.050 field devices ─approx. 2.700 physical and communicative data points; production, provision, adaptation and final dismantling of the temporary electrical site power supply for construction execution. This includes feed-in, site power main and sub-distribution boards, wiring networks, connection points, lighting, and required testing. ─approx. 9 site power main and site power sub-distribution boards ─approx. 700 m of temporary cable and wiring networks ─approx. 45 temporary luminaires; production, provision and dismantling of the temporary site water supply, including connection to the existing drinking water network, temporary pipe routing, extraction points, system separation and required frost protection measures. ─approx. 100 m of temporary site water pipe ─2 site water connections with multiple extraction options each ─1 system separators ─approx. 50 m of trace heating including control ─provision, adaptation and dismantling of the temporary system

