The purpose of this contract relates to the provision of services by these technical experts, mainly on a time-and-materials basis under the control of the contracting authority, which acts as project manager. A minority of services relates to fixed-price service provision. Projects are carried out by the contracting authority in numerous areas of Information and Communication Management. The projects evolve rapidly and are mainly linked to application development and system-technical aspects. To successfully carry out these numerous projects, the contracting authority wishes to call upon technical experts in the field of information and communication technologies (ICT). The purpose of this contract relates to the provision of services by these technical experts, mainly on a time-and-materials basis under the control of the contracting authority, which acts as project manager. A minority of services relates to fixed-price service provision. Within the framework of this SCC, the needs for technical expertise are divided into 26 distinct IT activity areas or professions which correspond to the 26 lots. For each lot, the framework agreement will be concluded with the economic operators submitting the regular tenders (up to a maximum of 5 tenders, provided that the number of tenders received permits this) that are the most economically advantageous on the basis of the award criterion.Projects are carried out by the contracting authority in numerous areas of Information and Communication Management. The projects evolve rapidly and are mainly linked to application development and system-technical aspects. To successfully carry out these numerous projects, the contracting authority wishes to call upon technical experts in the field of information and communication technologies (ICT). The purpose of this contract relates to the provision of services by these technical experts, mainly on a time-and-materials basis under the control of the contracting authority, which acts as project manager. A minority of services relates to fixed-price service provision. Within the framework of this SCC, the needs for technical expertise are divided into 26 distinct IT activity areas or professions which correspond to the 26 lots. For each lot, the framework agreement will be concluded with the economic operators submitting the regular tenders (up to a maximum of 5 tenders, provided that the number of tenders received permits this) that are the most economically advantageous on the basis of the award criterion.; As network activities are diverse and varied, they have been grouped by competence area: • DNS, DHCP and IP services • Firewall service • Remote Access (VPN) service • Load Balancer service • IDS/IPS service • WebGateway (proxy) service • Wifi service • LAN/MAN/WAN and datacenter network service Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Monitoring and coordination of the management of an IT management process: changes, incidents, problems, releases, configurations (CMDB), continuity, service catalogue • Operational management of the process: evaluate and check requests, monitor them, coordinate them, monitor and check the backlog, draft reports, etc. • Monitoring of service management and in particular compliance with SLAs; • Undertaking the revision and evolution (including optimisation) of IT management processes: changes, incidents, problems, releases, configurations (CMDB), continuity, service catalogue • Process owner: define and improve the process; define KPIs/CSFs, calculate them, monitor their evolution; guarantee the proper functioning of the process; etc. Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Provide first-tier helpdesk intervention/local support to information system users. • Provide second-tier helpdesk for issues caused by business applications. • Provide functional assistance on the Office suite (macros, templates, scripting, dbAccess) • Perform the tasks of any local IT correspondent of the SPW. • Execute periodic information system support operations (collection/analysis of logs, resource availability, log analyses, etc.). • Administer/manage certain branches of Active Directory. Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; General activities: • Administer the SPW BI platforms (servers, profiles and users). • Manage the data integration environment. • Assistance with the deployment and configuration of BI systems. • Provide basic or advanced training (coaching) to users on the BI tools deployed at the SPW. • Advise the business and provide support to users of the various platforms. • Bring expertise to the team that they will join. Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years;

• Identify UX/UI requirements through user research • Translate complex problems into simple interfaces (user flows, wireframes and prototypes) that lead to intuitive user experiences • Contribute to service design by proposing user-oriented solutions using a co-creation approach (design thinking, UX design) • Design effective and accessible interfaces for various websites and applications, complying with the graphic design standards and drawing inspiration from best practices • Document interfaces by describing styles, typography, illustrations, information architecture, interactions and navigation • Draw up user test scenarios, identify key problems and make recommendations to resolve them • Participate in the building and evolution of the Design System to ensure user experience consistency across the various digital products of SPW • Participate in every stage of digital application construction (brainstorming, user research, prototypes, user tests, implementation) • Work closely with other project roles (UX designer, Product Owner, Scrum Master, developer, testers, etc.) so that UX/UI is smoothly integrated into the agile process • Maintain regular and effective communication with the project team and the business throughout the projects • Create concepts and translate them into wireframes to design services and user experiences based on user research and using design-thinking methodologies and techniques (UX design) • Bring new ideas with high added value for users and the organisation Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Ensure technical supervision of the deployment of Alfresco to potentially 12000 users (compliance with specifications set out via the architecture study, control of instantiations, performance verification, etc.). • Install, configure and integrate new versions of Alfresco solutions with developments currently carried out by SPW Digital on the Alfresco version 5.1. • Develop deterministic workflows. • Integrate the Alfresco EDRMS solution with the office suite, the digitisation tool, the standard CMS (Jahia) and potentially with other EDRMS tools, etc. • Provide administrator and user training for the Alfresco solution. • Enhance the skills of the SPW Digital EDRMS technical team. • Analyse and program new functional specifications. • Perform technical analysis based on functional analysis in order to best integrate it into the Alfresco solution, complying with SPW Digital architectural standards. • Program and test solution-related features. • Help manage SPW Digital internal EDRMS managers and guide them in technical choices. • Start programming certain features in order to pass them on to an internal EDRMS manager at SPW Digital. • Provide skills in Solr, Java, Javascript, etc., to improve team knowledge and the Alfresco solution. • Produce functional documentation (user guides, etc.) and technical documentation. • Respond to specific requirements by integrating them into the solution with Alfresco. • Contribute to making the solution more ergonomic. • Assist with the migration of existing data. • Provide skills in change management, communication and training for the deployment of the EDRMS solution. • Support EDRMS users. • Ensure that Alfresco is fully operational within SPW with the help of SPW Digital IT operations managers. • Report and track incidents or questions with Alfresco support • Participate in architectural recommendations for the Alfresco solution. • Consultants assigned to the mission must master the CMIS protocol. • Consultants assigned to the mission must have an in-depth command of the Alfresco solution (installation, configuration, integration with business applications and repositories) as well as a command of the technical environment specific to the mission. Furthermore, they must be certified by Alfresco. • Consultants assigned to the mission must provide support for technology watch regarding the Alfresco solution. Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; SPW Digital uses content management systems (CMS) for intranet and internet sites deployed within SPW. The main software for this implementation is Jahia given its integration into SPW's technical environment (Java development);. In many cases, developments are necessary to integrate these CMS tools with specific business needs. SPW Digital also encourages the use of this software for the administration's cross-functional needs. Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Manage specific (business-requested) and/or cross-functional IT projects efficiently (management of budget, time, scope, quality, risks, changes, constraints, stakeholders and communication). Participate in the implementation and improvement of a project management tool intended for SPW project managers. • Support a department in implementing project governance • Provide training and coaching in project monitoring. • Ensure the management of interdependencies between projects. • Ensure the allocation of human and other resources across the various projects. Organise a portfolio management of projects, programmes and/or plans • Actively participate in the activities of the Project Management Office. • Definition of management and/or quality processes within SPW Digital. Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years;

• Manage IT, data exchange or authentic source labelling projects efficiently (budget, time, scope, quality, risk, change, constraint, stakeholder and communication management). • Understand the architecture and functionality of an information system. • Provide support to business project managers collaborating on the projects managed. • Produce or contribute to the production of project progress reports. • Implement management and/or quality processes within SPW Digital. • Interact with business teams and service providers involved in the project. • Draft administrative documents (memos, minutes, reports, letters, etc.). • Present projects developed orally and/or in writing using communication media (visual, written, audiovisual, etc.). Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Ensure adaptive and corrective maintenance of the ITSM tool and its installed modules. • Ensure adaptive and corrective maintenance of interfaces with other components (LDAP, inventory tool, discovery tool, urbi, etc.). • Integrate the ITSM tool with other tools and data sources, for both the ITSM tool and its CMDB. • Ensure adaptive and corrective maintenance of the discovery tool. • Provide user training on the various modules of the ITSM tools and their various modules. • Offer support for tool administration. • Provide technology watch advice on new products or new product versions likely to improve the operation of SPW IT services. Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Analyse and design technical architectures for the development of web-oriented applications (intranet, internet). • Analyse and design technical architectures (service-oriented) for the development of multi-tier and client-server applications. • Assist in setting up and configuring the software infrastructures of the architectures in the various environments (development, test, production, etc.). • Provide technical and methodological support to development teams. • Ensure coordination between functional analysts and developers to ensure alignment between the architectural solution and functional requirements. • Conduct a technology watch of the architectures in place. Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Participate in VoIP telephony evolution projects by: o Configuring and installing VoIP telephony equipment according to user needs and existing VoIP telephony standards o Advising users based on VoIP telephony features o Contacting and coordinating various telephony providers (tracking orders and invoices) o Ensuring the monitoring of installations and de-installations/decommissioning o Producing or modifying existing documentation (reports/diagrams/procedures) o Adapting stock inventories and inventory tools (CMDB) • Participate in mobile telephony evolution and deployment projects by: o Assessing needs with users; o Advising users o Configuring and installing mobile telephony equipment (GSM, smartphones and tablets) o Establishing procedures for users and the telephony unit o Using mobile device management tools (MAM, MDM) • Participate in the daily operations specific to fixed (traditional and VoIP) and mobile telephony infrastructures: o incident management o change management o monitoring tool surveillance o order and delivery processing • Report on tasks and activities (progress status, issues encountered, etc.) to the unit manager Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Ensure the management and administrative or technical follow-up of requests for material and immaterial equipment (licences) originating from internal clients (handling and analysis of purchase requests, supporting internal clients in defining their requirements, providing information on the progress of files, drawing up and implementing equipment plans, etc.) while ensuring quality at every stage of the procedure, including the preparation of specifications and technical opinions, as well as the drafting of administrative documents (letters, minutes, memos, reports, etc.) • Maintain the inventory of assets and contracts for the supply of material and immaterial goods or services (software user licences and maintenance services) and ensure their follow-up: file status, reminders to stakeholders, appointment scheduling • Prepare specific acquisition request files not included in the catalogue • Ensure administrative management and logistical processing of tasks relating to the management of orders, stock, deliveries and the installation of material goods, consumables and software • Publish and update a catalogue listing materials/consumables and software products • Manage contracts and markets for which the unit is responsible and monitor their execution • Ensure the selection of supplier products based on objective criteria respecting public procurement regulations • Maintain knowledge of the market, suppliers and products, and conduct market research • Create and maintain an excellent relationship with various stakeholders • Provide support for internal clients regarding the fulfilment of their requests • Ensure a good relationship with publishers Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; o Develop, perform design analysis and maintain applications in a client-server, web or mobile architecture.

o Participate in the design analysis of modules to be developed. Develop and perform unit tests. o Participate in code review sessions. o Ensure knowledge transfer by drafting technical documentation. o Control source code management, deployment and package build mechanisms. o Assist with incident and change management. Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Acquire necessary and sufficient business knowledge. • Document, model and analyse business processes and procedures as well as business entities. • Identify and use business concepts and business rules. • Understand and analyse user needs. • Define the scope of the information system (identification of actors, identification and description of use cases, data and any other relevant element for the information system). • Capture, elicit, analyse, validate and manage functional and non-functional business requirements while respecting the requirement classification and formalism established in the methodology used at SPW-Digital, which implies the reuse of 'standard' or 'cross-functional' requirements and requirement traceability. • Draft the project requirements specification. • Produce and document the functional analysis of the project. • Draft and execute functional test scenarios and test plans. • Draft user documentation and online help. • Carry out administrative and legal procedures necessary for the proper execution of the project (e.g. request for access to an authentic source). • Provide user training, presentations and various demos. • Assist users during the start-up and testing phases. • Lead and/or participate in management meetings (project steering committee, etc.). Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Participate in maintaining a coherent process and case management architecture; • Maintain a coherent repository of processes, case types, data models, etc.; • Analyse case types and processes with the business and model them; • Supervise and assist functional analysts in modelling; • Assist the business in optimising its processes (redesign, simulations); • Perform technical analyses based on functional analyses or requirements specifications; • Design processes and case types taking into account the technical elements necessary for their automation; • Produce functional and technical documentation; • Promote the process and case management architecture to the business. Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Provide techno-operational knowledge in Identity and Access Management. • Configure Identity and Access Management [IAM] products in the technical environment. • Develop missing functionality where appropriate. • Analyse incidents and problems; propose and implement corrections. • Guarantee data integrity and system consistency with various authentic sources and clients. Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Implement and manage web services. • Implement and manage inter-application messaging services. • Implement and manage ESB-type and related services such as a web service catalogue, data schema catalogue, etc. • Implement and manage data integration services (ETL, KAFKA, etc.). • Carry out these implementations within a continuous integration environment. • Help set up and configure software infrastructures in various environments (development, test, production, etc.). • Provide technical support to development teams. • Assist the Service Desk in managing incidents on SOA elements. Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; Without being exhaustive, this will involve leading, contributing to or performing one or more of the following activities in these areas: Governance Risk Compliance (GRC): • Determine security requirements for systems or applications (project mode or maintenance), ensure they are implemented; • Translate security policies into standards, procedures and recommendations. • Based on context and technology watch, identify needs and propose improvements to existing SPW Information System Security policies (To be); • Define and adapt a risk management methodology based on frameworks, conduct risk analyses and propose treatment plans; • Provide support, coaching or advice on security; Protection and defence: • Implement security solutions or measures; • Manage information system vulnerabilities or weaknesses and propose remediations or countermeasures; • Define and execute a security awareness programme (communication, training, etc.); • Security event and incident management. Conceptualisation and modelling: • Define and model relationships between infrastructure or solution components (to be); • Contribute to solution architecture or design on security aspects (security by design, SSDLC, DevSecOps); • Model and conceptualise an information system security architecture to guarantee defence in depth, among other things. Analysis and audit: • Analyse SPW information system elements or procedures from a security perspective (As is); • Conduct organisational or technical compliance audits; • For a defined scope, design, implement and present security-related queries and reports; establish an indicator dashboard (tableau); analyse and publish the results;

• Carry out intrusion testing assignments within the SPW IT system across defined perimeters (such as Blackbox, GreyBox or WhiteBox pentesting). Total duration of the lot: 6 (4+1+1) years; • Participate in the transversal quality approach regarding the organisation of IT developments and the services provided within SPW Digital. • Help select priority processes to which the quality approach will be applied and assist with their modelling. • Help manage quality based on user feedback and information on service delivery in order to define and/or adapt reference documents. • Deploy and support continuous improvement within SPW Digital. • Propose metrics (qualitative and quantitative) and implement them before and after the rollout of the improvement approach to measure changes. • Set up and monitor quality control actions, particularly regarding deliverables provided both internally and by service providers. • Actively participate in the various communities of practice.
